course: dictionary
lesson: 12926
title: Evaluate: judge and work it out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To evaluate something is to judge how good, useful or successful it is, after you think about it carefully. It means more than saying "I liked it": you look at the reasons. «We will evaluate our paper planes after the test flight.» You would think about which plane flew furthest and why.
explain: In maths, evaluate is an instruction word. It means work out the value as a number. «Evaluate 3 × (4 + 2).» Do the bracket first: 4 + 2 = 6. Then 3 × 6 = 18, so the value is 18.
explain: Look for the words next to evaluate. «Evaluate your work» means say what went well and what could be better. «Evaluate the evidence» means weigh up how strong each piece of evidence is. The clue words tell you what kind of thinking to do.
fact: Evaluate is a verb: evaluate, evaluates, evaluated, evaluating.
fact: «Evaluate» means to judge how good, useful or successful something is, after careful thought.
fact: In maths, «evaluate» means work out the value of an expression as a number.
fact: «Evaluate your work» means say what went well and what could be better.
fact: «Evaluate the evidence» means weigh up how strong it is before you decide.
exercise: «We will evaluate our paper planes after the test flight.» What does evaluate mean here? | Throw them away straight after | *Judge how good they were, after thinking carefully | Paint them in bright colours | Count how many folds they have
exercise: «Evaluate 3 × (4 + 2).» What is the value? | 24 | 12 | 9 | *18
exercise: In reading, why would you evaluate a website before you use it? | To make it look more colourful | *To check whether it is reliable | To print it quickly | To count how many words it has
test: «Sam had to evaluate his science experiment.» What should Sam do? | Hide it from the teacher | Finish it as fast as he can | Copy a friend's experiment | *Say what went well and what could be better
test: «Evaluate 5 + 2 × 3.» What is the value? | 21 | 16 | *11 | 15
exam: «The team had to evaluate the evidence before deciding.» What does evaluate mean here? | Read the evidence aloud very quickly | Ignore the evidence completely | Lose the evidence in the bin | *Weigh up how strong the evidence is
